[[:db/retract 17592186117861 :answer-field/choices 17592186117862] [:db/retract 17592186117861 :answer-field/choices 17592186117863] [:db/retract 17592186117861 :answer-field/choices 17592186117864] [:db/retract 17592186117861 :answer-field/choices 17592186117865] [:db/retract 17592186117861 :answer-field/choices 17592186117866] {:db/id 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d79c5095-b4c8-55c2-88ef-92a621d4625c" "question-16cdbada-67e8-5de1-a9af-81171c0d9ab3" "question-3ffd9e9c-d842-5a8a-82a2-58996823be61"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7ba59ca0-21f4-55ed-9a11-93e0f28f7d7a" "question-1147fbce-b0d6-511f-b878-2ccccfbc032b" "question-6c7e6c99-f8ae-5d4a-9e7f-5c595417e9ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a07b5060-561f-5345-8fe4-ea776cd5863a" "question-f674176f-f4e0-51c5-b4b9-0830e520af3b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d79c5095-b4c8-55c2-88ef-92a621d4625c" :question/id #uuid "d79c5095-b4c8-55c2-88ef-92a621d4625c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34887" :question/problem "Consider the curve  $r(t)=(6t-6)\\,i+4(t-1)^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=4{t}^{3/2}.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parameterization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since  $s=4{t}^{3/2}$,  we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =4{t}^{3/2} \\\\ {t}^{3/2} & =\\frac{s}{4} \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =[6{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-6]\\,i+4{[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k \\\\  & =6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]\\,i+4{[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93649b9b-4496-5be5-8efe-dc54d74802dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93649b9b-4496-5be5-8efe-dc54d74802dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "93649b9b-4496-5be5-8efe-dc54d74802dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21552ed1-365f-5f5f-9f16-05c0709bc3e6" "answer-bece495d-d450-5992-940a-15e713087f67" "answer-3329a212-2843-5cea-8b79-3333d2a3bf2b" "answer-9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" "answer-63ae5483-af4f-5b7e-81e0-1879fd88e830"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21552ed1-365f-5f5f-9f16-05c0709bc3e6" :answer/id #uuid "21552ed1-365f-5f5f-9f16-05c0709bc3e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3[{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{3/4}-1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bece495d-d450-5992-940a-15e713087f67" :answer/id #uuid "bece495d-d450-5992-940a-15e713087f67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{[{(\\frac{s}{4}+1)}^{2/3}+1]}^{3/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3329a212-2843-5cea-8b79-3333d2a3bf2b" :answer/id #uuid "3329a212-2843-5cea-8b79-3333d2a3bf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{[{(\\frac{s}{4}-1)}^{2/3}+1]}^{2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" :answer/id #uuid "9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63ae5483-af4f-5b7e-81e0-1879fd88e830" :answer/id #uuid "63ae5483-af4f-5b7e-81e0-1879fd88e830" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{3/2}+1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-16cdbada-67e8-5de1-a9af-81171c0d9ab3" :question/id #uuid "16cdbada-67e8-5de1-a9af-81171c0d9ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-127693" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2}.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $y$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})-3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})-\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $y$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b84fca7e-39f0-5846-a5a5-8d1c1f76b531"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b84fca7e-39f0-5846-a5a5-8d1c1f76b531" :answer-field/id #uuid "b84fca7e-39f0-5846-a5a5-8d1c1f76b531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e86fc481-fc66-5c0e-8cd5-654a6782aa39" "answer-eeb7902b-1060-5a35-9399-e7e8e0a37d2b" "answer-0078bb74-f290-5ea7-a214-52b9d695f5aa" "answer-bdd6f943-95f7-5873-b8a8-4d4dc0f6b355" "answer-90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e86fc481-fc66-5c0e-8cd5-654a6782aa39" :answer/id #uuid "e86fc481-fc66-5c0e-8cd5-654a6782aa39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eeb7902b-1060-5a35-9399-e7e8e0a37d2b" :answer/id #uuid "eeb7902b-1060-5a35-9399-e7e8e0a37d2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0078bb74-f290-5ea7-a214-52b9d695f5aa" :answer/id #uuid "0078bb74-f290-5ea7-a214-52b9d695f5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdd6f943-95f7-5873-b8a8-4d4dc0f6b355" :answer/id #uuid "bdd6f943-95f7-5873-b8a8-4d4dc0f6b355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/id #uuid "90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ffd9e9c-d842-5a8a-82a2-58996823be61" :question/id #uuid "3ffd9e9c-d842-5a8a-82a2-58996823be61" :question/math-academy-id "q-127692" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=12t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=12t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{12}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe722847-9990-513e-91c0-d8fbc2f2c414"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe722847-9990-513e-91c0-d8fbc2f2c414" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe722847-9990-513e-91c0-d8fbc2f2c414" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa66aa49-7286-5817-af4c-b29349ada577" "answer-9b9add6d-7ad1-521a-b998-2bbe4dbdbf01" "answer-ae297d72-79f9-5500-a313-64fff1a8859b" "answer-1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" "answer-18b22410-7856-5e1a-acc1-6826159d44dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa66aa49-7286-5817-af4c-b29349ada577" :answer/id #uuid "fa66aa49-7286-5817-af4c-b29349ada577" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b9add6d-7ad1-521a-b998-2bbe4dbdbf01" :answer/id #uuid "9b9add6d-7ad1-521a-b998-2bbe4dbdbf01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6s)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae297d72-79f9-5500-a313-64fff1a8859b" :answer/id #uuid "ae297d72-79f9-5500-a313-64fff1a8859b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{12}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{12})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer/id #uuid "1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18b22410-7856-5e1a-acc1-6826159d44dc" :answer/id #uuid "18b22410-7856-5e1a-acc1-6826159d44dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ba59ca0-21f4-55ed-9a11-93e0f28f7d7a" :question/id #uuid "7ba59ca0-21f4-55ed-9a11-93e0f28f7d7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127707" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2} & =s \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}+3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}\\,,1-{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3}+3,\\,\\frac{s}{3},\\,1-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s}{3}+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1-\\frac{2s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65648327-28cf-5416-8e2f-6a1fc5001bde"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65648327-28cf-5416-8e2f-6a1fc5001bde" :answer-field/id #uuid "65648327-28cf-5416-8e2f-6a1fc5001bde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74144c16-17c1-5293-9b2e-c5a9eeff8750" "answer-32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" "answer-74bae46f-6326-5411-928d-8a2bfd164ba4" "answer-e25ed8bf-2138-5064-9377-39d74381a566" "answer-5cbd1f61-356b-5e0e-97c4-264d421a9397"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74144c16-17c1-5293-9b2e-c5a9eeff8750" :answer/id #uuid "74144c16-17c1-5293-9b2e-c5a9eeff8750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" :answer/id #uuid "32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74bae46f-6326-5411-928d-8a2bfd164ba4" :answer/id #uuid "74bae46f-6326-5411-928d-8a2bfd164ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e25ed8bf-2138-5064-9377-39d74381a566" :answer/id #uuid "e25ed8bf-2138-5064-9377-39d74381a566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cbd1f61-356b-5e0e-97c4-264d421a9397" :answer/id #uuid "5cbd1f61-356b-5e0e-97c4-264d421a9397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1147fbce-b0d6-511f-b878-2ccccfbc032b" :question/id #uuid "1147fbce-b0d6-511f-b878-2ccccfbc032b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78437" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\sqrt{6}t,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,2\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de6079b3-a0dd-5241-b8ce-a969c300edc5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de6079b3-a0dd-5241-b8ce-a969c300edc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "de6079b3-a0dd-5241-b8ce-a969c300edc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6486f987-8f88-59d1-a346-9c83d923a1ac" "answer-a1d0d21b-45e7-55b2-a074-9a46fed29092" "answer-447ff6ac-8e33-53a7-a4b3-bb9df76bffb0" "answer-b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" "answer-a5c74af9-8ca2-5cca-a7be-75a239dd9ecc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6486f987-8f88-59d1-a346-9c83d923a1ac" :answer/id #uuid "6486f987-8f88-59d1-a346-9c83d923a1ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d0d21b-45e7-55b2-a074-9a46fed29092" :answer/id #uuid "a1d0d21b-45e7-55b2-a074-9a46fed29092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-447ff6ac-8e33-53a7-a4b3-bb9df76bffb0" :answer/id #uuid "447ff6ac-8e33-53a7-a4b3-bb9df76bffb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{14},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/id #uuid "b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5c74af9-8ca2-5cca-a7be-75a239dd9ecc" :answer/id #uuid "a5c74af9-8ca2-5cca-a7be-75a239dd9ecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c7e6c99-f8ae-5d4a-9e7f-5c595417e9ec" :question/id #uuid "6c7e6c99-f8ae-5d4a-9e7f-5c595417e9ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-78402" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=(3t-1)\\,i+2t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=4t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=4t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{4}.$  \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{4}) \\\\  & =(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}-1)i+(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4})j+(\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{4})k \\\\  & =(\\frac{3s-4}{4})i+\\frac{s}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{4}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s-4}{4})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{4})k \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de3dc3d1-7e1d-5412-9859-e96e904a13e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de3dc3d1-7e1d-5412-9859-e96e904a13e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de3dc3d1-7e1d-5412-9859-e96e904a13e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0b622e5-528f-57ff-bbcd-8e0d4e03bb0f" "answer-c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" "answer-69ca1aac-6b11-5376-9937-2208496cced2" "answer-e925d7f5-a15f-5b03-9457-e819bfb1f793" "answer-d7a63ea5-e82d-58f3-a26d-7d87b25fa26b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0b622e5-528f-57ff-bbcd-8e0d4e03bb0f" :answer/id #uuid "f0b622e5-528f-57ff-bbcd-8e0d4e03bb0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}i+\\frac{1}{8}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" :answer/id #uuid "c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69ca1aac-6b11-5376-9937-2208496cced2" :answer/id #uuid "69ca1aac-6b11-5376-9937-2208496cced2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e925d7f5-a15f-5b03-9457-e819bfb1f793" :answer/id #uuid "e925d7f5-a15f-5b03-9457-e819bfb1f793" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7a63ea5-e82d-58f3-a26d-7d87b25fa26b" :answer/id #uuid "d7a63ea5-e82d-58f3-a26d-7d87b25fa26b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a07b5060-561f-5345-8fe4-ea776cd5863a" :question/id #uuid "a07b5060-561f-5345-8fe4-ea776cd5863a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78400" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,k,$  $\\,t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))k \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,i-4\\cdot 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,j+3\\cdot 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,i-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,j+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(20\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))}^{2}+{(16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))}^{2}+{(12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{400{cos}^{2}⁡(4t)+256{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)+144{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{400[{cos}^{2}⁡(4t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)]} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}20\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =20u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $s=20t$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =20t \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{20}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})k \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dff45dea-1e54-5748-adfe-76155f49648f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dff45dea-1e54-5748-adfe-76155f49648f" :answer-field/id #uuid "dff45dea-1e54-5748-adfe-76155f49648f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-357c3fed-2573-5af2-9a74-38fdbb7e9536" "answer-eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" "answer-33d8185a-6a2a-5892-8eca-d2a40aec6d78" "answer-7e98db7f-69a7-535b-991b-a8a9c022916b" "answer-c8848381-e308-52a4-a707-2d321aed36f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-357c3fed-2573-5af2-9a74-38fdbb7e9536" :answer/id #uuid "357c3fed-2573-5af2-9a74-38fdbb7e9536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" :answer/id #uuid "eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33d8185a-6a2a-5892-8eca-d2a40aec6d78" :answer/id #uuid "33d8185a-6a2a-5892-8eca-d2a40aec6d78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e98db7f-69a7-535b-991b-a8a9c022916b" :answer/id #uuid "7e98db7f-69a7-535b-991b-a8a9c022916b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8848381-e308-52a4-a707-2d321aed36f9" :answer/id #uuid "c8848381-e308-52a4-a707-2d321aed36f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120287 :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=5t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{5}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\cdot \\frac{s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117861 :answer-field/correct "answer-cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4ac553f-f8dc-540a-b14f-5081633e4785" "answer-a7440719-45de-5623-a9fc-402f1704445f" "answer-687213da-1e26-52a8-97ee-db6e4936d9a1" "answer-03d35f72-203f-50ad-acf8-60daf8ec86f4" "answer-cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4ac553f-f8dc-540a-b14f-5081633e4785" :answer/id #uuid "a4ac553f-f8dc-540a-b14f-5081633e4785" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7440719-45de-5623-a9fc-402f1704445f" :answer/id #uuid "a7440719-45de-5623-a9fc-402f1704445f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5s),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5s)⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-687213da-1e26-52a8-97ee-db6e4936d9a1" :answer/id #uuid "687213da-1e26-52a8-97ee-db6e4936d9a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s\\sqrt{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s\\sqrt{5})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d35f72-203f-50ad-acf8-60daf8ec86f4" :answer/id #uuid "03d35f72-203f-50ad-acf8-60daf8ec86f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{10},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558" :answer/id #uuid "cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f674176f-f4e0-51c5-b4b9-0830e520af3b" :question/id #uuid "f674176f-f4e0-51c5-b4b9-0830e520af3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127733" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3/2},\\,1⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{1/2},\\,2{t}^{1/2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{1/2})}^{2}+{(2{t}^{1/2})}^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}t+4t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}} & =s \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{3s}{5} \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =⟨{({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3})}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3})}^{3/2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3s}{5},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-369bbd24-91f1-5851-8599-621408e0023b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-369bbd24-91f1-5851-8599-621408e0023b" :answer-field/id #uuid "369bbd24-91f1-5851-8599-621408e0023b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" "answer-caf2317e-01bb-53d6-bd84-e85f0344d156" "answer-88524411-7322-5c13-a0d6-4635b37af634" "answer-9cf6e55a-b413-5aa8-ab0c-0067c9c7f83b" "answer-c64215ca-c1b2-57b5-bdd6-c53bbb436663"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" :answer/id #uuid "e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf2317e-01bb-53d6-bd84-e85f0344d156" :answer/id #uuid "caf2317e-01bb-53d6-bd84-e85f0344d156" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\frac{2s}{3},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88524411-7322-5c13-a0d6-4635b37af634" :answer/id #uuid "88524411-7322-5c13-a0d6-4635b37af634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cf6e55a-b413-5aa8-ab0c-0067c9c7f83b" :answer/id #uuid "9cf6e55a-b413-5aa8-ab0c-0067c9c7f83b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{5}},\\,\\frac{2s}{\\sqrt{5}},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c64215ca-c1b2-57b5-bdd6-c53bbb436663" :answer/id #uuid "c64215ca-c1b2-57b5-bdd6-c53bbb436663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R(s)=⟨s,\\,\\frac{4s}{3},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121001 :tutorial/content "Consider the curve $C$ parametrized by the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 2\\sin t, \\: 2\\cos t, \\: \\sqrt{5} t\\rangle, \\qquad t \\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nFor any $t >0,$ the arc length $s$ of $C$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\sqrt{5}⟩‖\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡u+{sin}^{2}⁡u)+5}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{9}\\,du \\\\  & =3u{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $s= 3t,$ or equivalently $t = \\dfrac{s}{3}.$ \n\nNow, we can define a new vector function $\\mathbf{R}$ as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(s)= \\mathbf r\\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right), \\: 2\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right), \\: \\sqrt{5} \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right) \\right\\rangle .\n$$\n\nThe function $\\mathbf{R}(s)$ gives us the *same* curve $C,$ but this time it is parameterized by the arc length $s.$\n\nIn general, if $\\mathbf r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b]$ is a continuously differentiable vector function such that $\\mathbf r'(t )\\neq \\mathbf{0},$ then to parametrize it in terms of arc length we perform the following steps:\n\n1\\. Compute $s = \\displaystyle s(t) = \\int_a^t\\|\\mathbf r'(u)\\| \\, \\mathrm{d}u$\n\n2\\. Write $s = s(t)$ in the form $t=t(s)$\n\n3\\. Substitute $t=t(s)$ back into $\\mathbf r(t)$ to get $\\mathbf R(s)=\\mathbf r(t(s))$\n\n**Note:** One advantage of parametrizing a curve by its arc length is that the tangent vector is always a unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\left\\|\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf R}{\\textrm{d} s}\\right\\| = 1\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120037 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
